{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/duckdb/duckdb/pulls/25232","id":4415906682,"node_id":"PR_kwDOCEU65s8AAAABBzVjeg","html_url":"https://github.com/duckdb/duckdb/pull/25232","diff_url":"https://github.com/duckdb/duckdb/pull/25232.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/duckdb/duckdb/pull/25232.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/duckdb/duckdb/issues/25232","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/duckdb/duckdb/pulls/25232/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/duckdb/duckdb/pulls/25232/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/duckdb/duckdb/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/duckdb/duckdb/issues/25232/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/duckdb/duckdb/statuses/f36d22edd4efa2d4f6dd3ff5059a2f8419ca729c","number":25232,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Fix parallel CSV reader duplicate rows with \\r\\r\\n line endings","user":{"login":"alwaysprince05","id":218506877,"node_id":"U_kgDODQYmfQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/218506877?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alwaysprince05","html_url":"https://github.com/alwaysprince05","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alwaysprince05/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alwaysprince05/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alwaysprince05/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alwaysprince05/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alwaysprince05/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alwaysprince05/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alwaysprince05/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alwaysprince05/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alwaysprince05/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Fixes #25164\r\n\r\nProblem\r\n\r\nWhen a CSV file uses \\r\\r\\n line endings and is read in parallel mode, the parallel CSV reader emits duplicate rows. This happens when a buffer boundary splits a row terminator between its two \\r characters:\r\n\r\nThe previous buffer's scanner processes the first \\r and counts the row via AddRow().\r\nProcessOverBufferValue() then consumes the remaining \\r\\n from the new buffer, but after its CARRY_ON newline-consuming loop it falls through to the \"second buffer\" loop, which starts parsing the next row's data.\r\nAs a result, the next row is counted by both the current scanner (via ProcessExtraRow) and the next scanner, producing duplicate rows.\r\nFix\r\n\r\nIn ProcessOverBufferValue(), after the CARRY_ON newline-consuming while loop, return early when:\r\n\r\nNo cross-buffer value exists (over_buffer_string is empty)\r\nNewline characters were consumed\r\nThe previous buffer's scanner already fully counted the row (last_position > actual_size)\r\nThe first consumed character is \\r (distinguishing \\r\\r\\n from \\r\\n)\r\nThis prevents the function from falling through to the \"second buffer\" loop and double-counting the next row.\r\n\r\nTesting\r\n\r\nThe regression test (test/sql/copy/csv/parallel/test_rrrn_parallel.test) generates the CSV on the fly via COPY ... (FORMAT BLOB) — no committed data file. Its layout is engineered so the bug actually triggers: fixed 25-byte rows follow a 26-byte header, placing row 39's first \\r on the last byte of the 1024-byte buffer (offset 1023), so the buffer boundary splits the terminator as \\r | \\r\\n.\r\n\r\nVerified on a relassert build:\r\n\r\nWithout the fix, the test fails: parallel read returns 61 rows and id 40 is duplicated (sequential returns the correct 60)\r\nWith the fix, parallel and sequential both return exactly 60 rows\r\nAll parallel CSV tests pass with 0 regressions","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-09-01T20:11:58Z","updated_at":"2026-09-07T10:51:32Z","closed_at":"2026-09-07T10:48:57Z","merged_at":"2026-09-07T10:48:57Z","merge_commit_sha":"59ae0c6fb3f29369cfd0df124c76e9232181ef86","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"alwaysprince05:fix-int64-min-interval-negation","ref":"fix-int64-min-interval-negation","repo":{"id":1327862324,"node_id":"R_kgDOTyWSNA","name":"duckdb","full_name":"alwaysprince05/duckdb","owner":{"login":"alwaysprince05","id":218506877,"node_id":"U_kgDODQYmfQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/218506877?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alwaysprince05","html_url":"https://github.com/alwaysprince05","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alwaysprince05/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alwaysprince05/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alwaysprince05/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alwaysprince05/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alwaysprince05/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alwaysprince05/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alwaysprince05/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alwaysprince05/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alwaysprince05/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"private":false,"fork":true,"archived":false,"disabled":false,"description":"DuckDB is an analytical in-process SQL database management system","homepage":"http://www.duckdb.org","language":"C++","visibility":"public","is_template":false,"topics":[],"forks_count":0,"forks":0,"stargazers_count":0,"watchers_count":0,"watchers":0,"open_issues_count":0,"open_issues":0,"size":520240,"default_branch":"main","has_issues":false,"has_projects":true,"has_wiki":false,"has_pages":false,"has_downloads":false,"has_discussions":false,"has_pull_requests":true,"pushed_at":"2026-10-02T20:11:30Z"